				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12436941#post-4833768</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12436941/three-moons-initiative-hub#post-4833768</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 01 Dec 2020 17:34:10 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Joshua Aaron</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>5612221</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>One of the SCPs I am currently planning to write is a high-powered thaumaturgist (named Quinn), and he was killed in an alternate universe. The GoC and Horizon Initiative (horizon initiative because he has ties to a religious organization that worships deities of magic) breached Quinn's containment and killed him before Nine Tail Fox could intervene and eliminate the invading GoC and HI soldiers. After that, he went to corbenic, and, since he was actually a good-aligned human who didn't do anything immoral, he didn't get punished. He immediately realized that his thaumaturgist powers worked in this afterlife, and that he could even summon his cat familiar still.</p> <p>After that, he slowly started to realized that the Three Moons Initiatives' leader (or more like leaders) are kinda tyrannical dictators, and many shared that sentiment. He managed to effectively cancel out their deity's powers with an anti-magic fields (see high-powered thaumaturgist), and even managed to create stuff similar to Scranton Realist Anchors, rendering all anomalous abilities and weaponry. He also destroyed a lot of military weapons and equipment in the process, and stole what he could for his fellow revolters.</p> <p>I plan to mention these events in a seperate SCP, as well as in a tale. The SCP entry given basics and scraps of info, while the tale would basically be an &quot;explanation&quot; entry.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
