				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12436941#post-4349716</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12436941/three-moons-initiative-hub#post-4349716</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 03 Sep 2019 21:11:46 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>AnomalousPotato</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2364855</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Critique</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Never&nbsp;thought&nbsp;I’d&nbsp;be&nbsp;considering&nbsp;a&nbsp;machine&nbsp;being&nbsp;inorganic&nbsp;as&nbsp;a&nbsp;maybe...&nbsp;the&nbsp;SCP&nbsp;wiki&nbsp;truly&nbsp;is&nbsp;a&nbsp;magical&nbsp;place.&nbsp;</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p>Inorganic matter is incapable of leaving Corbenic. As such, the majority of objects associated with the Three Moons Initiative are drones and other machines remote-controlled from Corbenic.</p> </blockquote> <p>If I’m reading this right, shouldn’t it be “Organic matter is incapable of leaving Corbenic”? With the majority being drones, how do they get there, assuming they’re inorganic?</p> </div> </div> </div> <p>Minor confusion aside, I’m glad to see that Three Moons has its own hub now! I’ll be interested to see where this goes. +1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
